\subsection{Source-Reachable Path Lyapunov Certificate}
\label{sec:stability-widening-source-path}

The quantitative Live certificate is built only on jointly source-reachable
execution words. It is not a Cartesian switching certificate and it does not
introduce a common Euclidean metric, a repeated one-step contraction argument,
or a replay-fitted acceptance pattern. Held-bias and active-bias operation are
proved separately in their fixed dimensions, 18 and 21, respectively; bias
release, magnetic re-gauging, tilt re-lock, and other dimension/reference/reset
events remain explicit hybrid obligations.

Every quantitative normal-Live word contains the recurring vector-PE event of
the deployment hypothesis and the complete translational qualification. For
translation, four usable $S=0$ updates observe the complete $(v,p,S,a_w)$ chain.
If $q_W$ is the largest spread index that fits in a word, the determinant
argument is valid for every integer $1\le q\le q_W$. The validated producer
therefore chooses
\begin{equation}
 q_W^*\in\arg\max_{1\le q\le q_W}\underline\lambda_{S,W}(q),
 \label{eq:widen-optimal-S-spread}
\end{equation}
where the rigorous lower bound includes both the $(q\Delta_{S,-})^6$ separation
benefit and the corresponding OU-decay/conditioning penalty. The three-$S$
detectability construction may sharpen a covariance upper bound when the stable
$a_w$ direction is treated separately, but it is not a theorem-promotion
fallback for the four-$S$ complete-chain qualification.

\subsubsection{Source graph and exact homogeneous information geometry}

For each mode $m\in\{H,A\}$ let
\begin{equation}
 \mathscr G_{{\rm src},m}=(\mathscr M_m,\mathscr E_m)
 \label{eq:widen-src-graph}
\end{equation}
cover the source-reachable covariance, scheduler, pseudo-measurement phase,
accepted/rejected update state, magnetic state, and committed OU/$R_S$
parameters. An edge $e=(i,j)$ carries the compact family
\begin{equation}
 \mathscr A_e=\{A_{k,m}^{\rm cl}:\hbox{the source can move from $i$ to $j$}\}.
 \label{eq:widen-src-edge-family}
\end{equation}
For a graph word $w=(i_0,e_0,\ldots,e_{r-1},i_r)$ define
\begin{equation}
 \mathscr P_w=
 \left\{\Phi_w=A_{r-1}\cdots A_0:
 A_s\in\mathscr A_{e_s},\ \hbox{the complete tuple is jointly source reachable}
 \right\}.
 \label{eq:widen-src-word-family}
\end{equation}
The word family $\mathscr W_{{\rm src},m}$ has bounded length
\begin{equation}
 1\le\ell_-\le\ell(w)\le\ell_+<\infty
 \label{eq:widen-src-word-length}
\end{equation}
and is source complete when every infinite same-mode execution can be tiled by
such words. At an arbitrary word entrance the full invariant applied-parameter
box is retained unless source history proves a combination unreachable; in
particular, the separate $R_S$ smoothing memory prevents deleting entrance
corners merely from the instantaneous target law.

Let $\Sigma_i\succ0$ denote the estimator covariance at source node $i$. P3
proves directly on every source-complete word that
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{\Phi_w^\top\Sigma_{i_r}^{-1}\Phi_w
 \preceq(1-\delta_w)\Sigma_{i_0}^{-1},\qquad \delta_w>0,}
 \label{eq:widen-path-information-word}
\end{equation}
without multiplying one-sample decreases. The exact covariance decomposition
$\Sigma_s=\Phi_s\Sigma_0\Phi_s^\top+\Omega_s$, $\Omega_s\succeq0$, also gives
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{\Phi_s^\top\Sigma_s^{-1}\Phi_s\preceq\Sigma_0^{-1}}
 \label{eq:widen-path-prefix}
\end{equation}
for every source-reachable prefix. Thus a homogeneous segment is nonexpansive
in its matching source information metrics even though individual samples need
not decrease any common scalar energy.

For numerical normalization choose one positive constant $s_m$ for the entire
fixed-dimensional mode and set
\begin{equation}
 M_i:=s_m\Sigma_i^{-1},\qquad i\in\mathscr M_m.
 \label{eq:widen-path-information-metric}
\end{equation}
The implementation certificate takes
$s_m=\overline\lambda(\Sigma)_m$, the source-uniform covariance eigenvalue upper
bound. The same $s_m$ is used at every node in mode $m$, so this rescaling can
neither manufacture path contraction nor change a physical level set. It only
keeps the reported $W$ levels numerically well scaled. If
\begin{equation}
 m_-I\preceq M_i\preceq m_+I,
 \label{eq:widen-path-P-bounds}
\end{equation}
then the chosen normalization gives a source-certified $m_->0$ while retaining
the complete attitude--linear information cross terms. Multiplying
Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-path-information-word} by the common positive $s_m$ leaves
its generalized contraction ratio unchanged.

\begin{theorem}[Source-complete homogeneous information-word stability]
\label{thm:widen-path-ues}
Suppose $\mathscr W_{{\rm src},m}$ is source complete, the covariance metric
bounds of Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-path-P-bounds} hold, and every certified word
satisfies Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-path-information-word} with $\delta_w>0$. Then
the homogeneous fixed-mode recursion is uniformly exponentially stable on all
source-reachable executions in that mode. No decrease is required at an
individual sample inside the word.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
With $V_i(z)=z^\top M_i z$, Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-path-information-word} gives
$V_{i_r}(\Phi_w z)\le(1-\delta_w)V_{i_0}(z)$. Source completeness tiles every
same-mode execution with bounded-length contracting words, while
Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-path-prefix} supplies the finite intermediate-prefix gain.
\end{proof}

\subsubsection{Exact Cayley lift to $\SO(3)$}

On the geodesic chart $0\le\theta<\pi$, define the exact Cayley coordinate
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{c(R_e):=2\tan\!\left(\frac{\theta_e}{2}\right)u_e
       =\frac{4e_R}{1+\operatorname{tr}R_e}.}
 \label{eq:widen-path-cayley-coordinate}
\end{equation}
It is smooth and one-to-one on the chart, with differential
$dc|_{R=I}=d\theta$. For $z_C=(c(R_e),\xi)$ define
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{W_i(R_e,\xi):=z_C^\top M_i z_C
 =s_m z_C^\top\Sigma_i^{-1}z_C.}
 \label{eq:widen-path-group-metric}
\end{equation}
Unlike the retired block-diagonal lift, Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-path-group-metric}
retains all source information cross terms between attitude and the linear
coordinates. Its local quadratic is exactly the P3 information geometry up to
the single mode-global positive scalar $s_m$; hence no condition-number
conversion is inserted between P3 and P4.

The exact Cayley rotation is
\begin{equation}
 R(c)=I+\frac{4}{4+\|c\|^2}[c]_\times
       +\frac{2}{4+\|c\|^2}[c]_\times^2,
 \label{eq:widen-path-cayley-rotation}
\end{equation}
and for $\|c\|\le1$,
\begin{equation}
 \|R(c)-I-[c]_\times\|_2\le\frac34\|c\|^2.
 \label{eq:widen-path-cayley-remainder}
\end{equation}
The implemented correction is not replaced by an exponential approximation.
For $\|d\|<10^{-2}$ the source calls its normalized polynomial quaternion with
\begin{equation}
 w(d)=1-\frac{\|d\|^2}{8}+\frac{\|d\|^4}{384},\qquad
 k(d)=\frac12-\frac{\|d\|^2}{48}+\frac{\|d\|^4}{3840},
 \label{eq:widen-path-source-series-quaternion}
\end{equation}
and the corresponding exact correction Cayley vector is $c_d=(2k/w)d$. The
validated arithmetic encloses this source branch directly. Outside that branch
the source axis--angle quaternion is likewise enclosed directly; the final
inner P4 level proves every accepted correction remains on the polynomial
branch, so no branch fallback is needed.

For two finite Cayley vectors the exact left-product identity is
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{c(R_dR)=\frac{c_d+c+\tfrac12c_d\times c}
      {1-\tfrac14c_d^\top c}.}
 \label{eq:widen-path-cayley-product}
\end{equation}
The denominator is explicitly bounded away from zero on the certified funnel.
This identity is used after every accepted $S$, accelerometer, and magnetometer
correction in the actual source order. In particular, a due $S=0$ correction
occurs inside \texttt{time\_update} before the accelerometer correction, and
each accepted correction performs its own quaternion injection and left-error
covariance reset immediately. The full $S\to\theta$ gain is retained.

Let the exact zero-input word map be
\begin{equation}
 (R_e^+,\xi^+)=\mathcal F_w(R_e,\xi,0).
 \label{eq:widen-path-nonlinear-lift}
\end{equation}
It composes exact prediction, due/not-due $S$, accepted/rejected accelerometer,
asynchronous not-due/accepted/rejected magnetometer, source parameter evolution,
immediate quaternion/reset operations, and PSD $a_w$ covariance synchronization.
Rejected branches contribute identity corrections; they are not deleted from
the source language.

Each implemented nonlinear state operation admits on a compact Cayley ball a
source-uniform defect representation
\begin{equation}
 z_{s+1}=A_s z_s+r_s(z_s),\qquad \|r_s(z_s)\|\le C\|z_s\|^2.
 \label{eq:widen-path-quadratic-defect}
\end{equation}
The constant $C$ is obtained from the exact Cayley residual and quaternion
bounds, the source physical-vector envelope, and the full Kalman-gain bound
$\|K\|\le\sqrt{\overline\lambda(\Sigma)/\underline\lambda(R)}$. Because
Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-path-prefix} transports every homogeneous suffix with
information gain at most one, the defects may appear at arbitrary admissible
branch positions without enumerating all rejection strings.

If $N_{\rm op}$ bounds the number of state operations in a word and the bootstrap
assumes $W_s\le4W_0$, then
\begin{equation}
 \|r_w\|_{M_{i_r}}\le B_m W_0,\qquad
 B_m:=\frac{4N_{\rm op}\sqrt{m_+}\,C}{m_-}.
 \label{eq:widen-path-word-defect}
\end{equation}
Choose the explicit inner level
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{\sqrt{W_{*,m}}\le\frac{\delta_m}{8B_m}.}
 \label{eq:widen-path-W-star}
\end{equation}
Then the nonlinear defect consumes at most $\delta_m/8$ in the square-root
metric and yields the direct positive-gap estimate
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{W_{i_r}(\mathcal F_w(e,0))
 \le W_{i_0}(e)-\frac{\delta_m}{2}W_{i_0}(e).}
 \label{eq:widen-path-direct-decrease}
\end{equation}
For the deployed numerical certificate $\delta_m$ is far below binary64 machine
epsilon, so the implementation stores the positive decrement $\delta_m/2$
directly; it does not evaluate $1-\delta_m/2$ and round the strict gap back to
one.

The same calculation implies every prefix is strictly inside the assumed
$4W_0$ bootstrap, the Cayley norm is below one, and therefore
$\theta_e<1<\pi$. It also proves every accepted correction norm is below
$10^{-2}$, closing the exact source quaternion branch. In active-bias mode the
configured normal-Live node satisfies $\|\hat b_a\|\le0.45\,\mathrm{m/s^2}$
while the shipping projection radius is $0.5\,\mathrm{m/s^2}$. The certified
inner error radius is smaller than the remaining $0.05\,\mathrm{m/s^2}$ margin,
so the exact projection branch inside P4 is the identity interior branch.
Saturated boundary states are an outer capture/hybrid obligation rather than a
silently linearized P4 state.

Define
\begin{equation}
 \mu_W:=\inf_{m,w,e\ne0}
 \frac{W_{i_0}(e)-W_{i_r}(\mathcal F_w(e,0))}
      {V_R(R_e)+\|\xi\|^2},
 \label{eq:widen-path-direct-margin}
\end{equation}
over the certified prefix-safe source family. Since
$V_R(R_e)\le\|c(R_e)\|^2$ and $W_i\ge m_-\|z_C\|^2$ on the chart,
Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-path-direct-decrease} gives
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{\mu_W\ge\frac{\delta_m}{2}m_->0.}
 \label{eq:widen-path-direct-condition}
\end{equation}

\begin{theorem}[Exact source-word Cayley practical ISS seed]
\label{thm:widen-path-direct-iss}
Suppose the source graph is complete in each fixed-dimensional normal-Live mode,
P3 supplies a strict source-word information margin $\delta_m>0$, and the
validated bounds above establish $W_{*,m}>0$ with every prefix inside its
declared source/chart domain. Then every zero-input same-mode word has the
strict endpoint decrease of Eq.~\eqref{eq:widen-path-direct-decrease}, hence
$\mu_W>0$. By compactness and continuity, sufficiently small bounded
deterministic input yields a practical-ISS estimate on a nonzero inner funnel.
Positive one-sample changes of $W_i$ are allowed inside a word.
\end{theorem}

\subsubsection{Verification contract}

The deployed P4 certificate reports, for both $H$ and $A$,
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{\{\mathscr G_{{\rm src},m},\mathscr W_{{\rm src},m},s_m,
 m_-,m_+,\theta_{*,m},W_{*,m},B_m,\mu_{W,m}\}.}
 \label{eq:widen-path-contract}
\end{equation}
Passing requires every reachable same-mode transition to be covered; the word
family to be source complete; recurring vector PE and optimized four-$S$
complete translation qualification to occur in each tile; exact shipping
operation order and immediate resets; outward-rounded continuous bounds; full
attitude--linear information cross terms; safe prefixes; $W_{*,m}>0$; and
$\mu_{W,m}>0$. Monte Carlo and dense trajectory sampling are diagnostics only
and may falsify a claimed level but cannot establish one. The construction
changes neither the estimator nor the adaptation law and is the sole
quantitative normal-Live certificate path.
